WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.357
A ratio compares quantities multiplicatively

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:08.229
Two red dots for every three blue dots describes a mixture with five dots altogether

00:00:08.229 --> 00:00:14.100
Red to blue is two to three, while red to total is two to five.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.761
Doubling every ingredient produces four red and six blue dots

00:00:19.761 --> 00:00:27.175
The total changes, but the relationship stays the same because both quantities share the same scale factor

00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:31.100
Altering only one ingredient would create a different mixture.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:41.011
An equivalent way to express this comparison is a unit rate: one and a half cups of blue per cup of red

00:00:41.011 --> 00:00:46.100
Units and order matter, because reversing the comparison gives a different reciprocal rate.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.586
A part-to-part ratio is not already a fraction of the whole

00:00:51.586 --> 00:00:55.772
To find the red fraction, combine both parts in the denominator

00:00:55.772 --> 00:01:01.100
This distinction prevents using two thirds when the actual red share is two fifths.
